{"name":"Strait Fog","hex":"#6f6a68","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"strait","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Narrow; restricted as to space or room; close.","Righteous, strict."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A narrow channel of water connecting two larger bodies of water.","A narrow pass, passage or street."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/strait"},{"term":"fog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick cloud that forms near the ground; the obscurity of such a cloud.","A mist or film clouding a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with or as if with fog.","To become obscured in condensation or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Strait","blocks":[{"text":"A strait is a water body connecting two seas or water basins. The surface water is, for the most part, at the same elevation on both sides and can flow through the strait in either direction, although the topography generally constricts the flow somewhat. In some straits, there is a dominant directional current. Most commonly, the strait is a narrow channel that lies between two land masses. Straits are loci for sediment accumulation, with sand-sized deposits usually occurring on the two strait exits, forming subaqueous fans or deltas. Some straits are not navigable because they are too narrow, too shallow, or due to the presence of a reef or archipelago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Strait.svg/330px-Strait.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait","wikidata":"Q37901"},{"title":"Fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals held in the air near the Earth's surface. Fog can be considered a type of low-lying cloud usually resembling stratus and is heavily influenced by nearby bodies of water, topography, and wind conditions. In turn, fog affects many human activities, such as shipping, travel, and warfare. Recent atmospheric research indicates that fog also functions as an active aquatic ecosystem. Fog droplets harbor microbiomes where bacteria actively grow, divide, and interact with atmospheric chemistry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg/330px-A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fog","wikidata":"Q37477"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg/500px-ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg/1280px-ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg/500px-ISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Strait of Gibraltar","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AISS-44_Strait_of_Gibraltar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg/500px-Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg/1280px-Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg/500px-Empty_Singapore-Malaysia_Causeway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Johor–Singapore Causeway tra